### VS Code ###
.vscode/

# AspectJ weaver crash dumps (see the aspectjweaver javaagent in pom.xml)
ajcore.*.txt

# Allure reports, one self-contained HTML file per run (see gmavenplus-plugin in pom.xml)
/reports/

# Worktrees an agent session creates for isolated work. Each one is a full checkout of this
# repository, so committing it would nest the repo inside itself, and `git add -A` will
# otherwise sweep one in. Remove a stale one with `git worktree remove`.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Per-machine operator settings for the "local" profile, layered over application.yaml by the
# "Local SpringApp" run configuration. It names one person's archive -- a path off their own
# machine -- so it never belongs in a commit, and putting it here rather than in
# src/main/resources also keeps it out of the packaged jar.
/application-local.yaml

# The working directory a run writes to: vespera.db and the operator's profile.yaml. The default is
# ${user.dir}/.vespera (see vespera.working-dir in application.yaml), so a run started from the repo
# root leaves it here. It is a real corpus's ledger -- file paths, hashes and verdicts from someone's
# own archive -- and it is per-machine state besides, so it never belongs in a commit.
/.vespera/
